From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] linker: the "symbol may need to be wrapped" hint only with linker debugging

The relocation of every pthread_* symbol that resolves to glibc's printed "symbol may need to be wrapped: <name>" to stderr, in
every process, at every load. A program's stderr is part of its output: Termux's bootstrap script reads `id -u 2>&1` and refused
the uid "symbol may need to be wrapped: pthread_self ... 1000". The hint is now a LINKER_DEBUG_PRINTF like the lines next to it.

apklayer patch 0034 of patches/bionic_translation.
---
diff --git a/linker/linker.c b/linker/linker.c
--- a/linker/linker.c
+++ b/linker/linker.c
@@ -1916,7 +1916,7 @@
 				// normal symbol
 			} else if ((sym_addr = (uintptr_t)dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT, sym_name))) {
 				if (strstr(sym_name, "pthread_"))
-					fprintf(stderr, "symbol may need to be wrapped: %s\n", sym_name);
+					LINKER_DEBUG_PRINTF("symbol may need to be wrapped: %s\n", sym_name);  /* apklayer patch: a hint for linker debugging; on stderr it is part of every program's output (`id -u 2>&1` in a script) */
 				LINKER_DEBUG_PRINTF("%s hooked symbol %s to %p\n", si->name, sym_name, (void *)sym_addr);
 			} else if (!sym_addr && !strncmp(sym_name, "gl", 2)) {
 				LINKER_DEBUG_PRINTF("=======================================\n");
